timeline
    title 3D AI Discoveries Timeline (2016–2026)
    section 2016–2018: Foundations
        2016 : 3D Semantic Parsing of Large-Scale Indoor Spaces
        2017 : ScanNet: Richly-Annotated 3D Reconstructions
        2018 : NeRF (Neural Radiance Fields)
              : Local Light Field Fusion
    section 2019–2021: Neural Representations & Self-Supervision
        2019 : Mip-NeRF, Neural 3D Video Synthesis
        2020 : nuScenes dataset, BlendedMVS
              : Score-based generative modeling
        2021 : DINO (self-supervised ViT)
              : CLIP (Vision-Language)
              : Mix3D (out-of-context augmentation)
    section 2022–2023: Diffusion & Foundation Models
        2022 : DINOv2, Latent Diffusion Models
              : Mip-NeRF 360, Neural 3D Video
        2023 : SAM (Segment Anything)
              : Scannet++ dataset
              : Open-Vocabulary 3D Segmentation
    section 2024–2025: Feed-Forward 3D & Gaussian Splatting
        2024 : Point Transformer V3
              : Open-Vocabulary 3D Semantic Segmentation
        2025 : Hot3D (hand/object tracking)
              : Uni3r, Volsplat, Flow3r, Gen3r
              : Depth Anything 3
    section 2026: Unified 3D Understanding
        2026 : Nova3r, SAM 3, OpenWorldSAM
              : Feed-forward 3D reconstruction
              : Memory-bounded 3D models
